module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Etale.DirectedColimitPresentation

/-!
# A quotient of a polynomial algebra is generated by the classes of the variables

Two `A`-algebra homomorphisms out of `A[x_i : i ∈ σ] ⧸ I` which agree on the class of every
variable are equal.

This is what pins down a homomorphism out of a presentation. The proof of Stacks 07SQ produces
its comparison morphism from an *existence* statement — the commutative-algebra core
`MvPolynomial.exists_ge_etale_surjective_quotient_of_directed` returns the identification of the
étale algebra with the presentation over the limit as a bare `Nonempty`, so the isomorphism it
provides is not pinned to anything — while the morphism whose base change has to be shown an
isomorphism is a *specific* one, built from `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coordinateHom`. The two are
reconciled by choosing the isomorphism, lifting the images of the classes of the variables under
its inverse to a finite stage, and then observing that the resulting `coordinateHom` and that
inverse agree on the classes of the variables, hence are equal. The last step is this lemma, and
without it the existence statement cannot be transported onto the specific morphism at all.

## Main results

* `MvPolynomial.algHom_ext_quotient`

## Implementation notes

Both halves are Mathlib's: `MvPolynomial.algHom_ext` for the polynomial algebra, and
`Ideal.Quotient.algHom_ext` for the quotient, the latter reducing equality of two maps out of
`A ⧸ I` to equality of their composites with `Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ`. Composing them is the whole
proof, and the only step with any content is that the composite of a map out of the quotient
with `Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ` sends a variable to the class of that variable, which is `simp`.

The hypothesis is stated with `Ideal.Quotient.mk` rather than with `Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ` because
the class of a polynomial is how a consumer has it:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coordinateHom_mk_X` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presentationStructureHom` are both written with `Ideal.Quotient.mk`.

Nothing here raises a compiler limit or disables a linter.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07SQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07SQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace MvPolynomial

/-- **A quotient of a polynomial algebra is generated by the classes of the variables.** Two
`A`-algebra homomorphisms out of `A[x_i : i ∈ σ] ⧸ I` agreeing on the class of every variable are
equal.

Equality of two maps out of the quotient is equality of their composites with
`Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ`, and two `A`-algebra homomorphisms out of a polynomial algebra agreeing on
every variable are equal. -/
theorem algHom_ext_quotient {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {σ : Type w}
    {I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A)} {R : Type v} [CommRing R] [Algebra A R]
    {f g : (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I) →ₐ[A] R}
    (h : ∀ k : σ, f (Ideal.Quotient.mk I (MvPolynomial.X k))
      = g (Ideal.Quotient.mk I (MvPolynomial.X k))) :
    f = g :=
  Ideal.Quotient.algHom_ext A (MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun k => by simpa using h k)

end MvPolynomial

end
